    {
      "id": "s_note_arg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 578,
      "y": 55,
      "width": 384,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 835822468,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 968648982,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790760489337,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "sketchpactId": "s_note_arg",
        "owner": "simplicity"
      },
      "text": "Change one variable at a time.\nD9 makes ESBMC the oracle:\nnative must match its verdicts\non tests/verify*. Inlining\n(c_emitter.rs:1159-1183) and\nBMC-only (contracts.md:36) are\ntoday's semantics. Modular calls\n(D4) and k-induction (D5) change\nverdicts, so a diff could not\ntell a native bug from a\nsemantics change. Swap the\nbackend first; change semantics\nlater, each with its own ADR.",
      "originalText": "Change one variable at a time. D9 makes ESBMC the oracle: native must match its verdicts on tests/verify*. Inlining (c_emitter.rs:1159-1183) and BMC-only (contracts.md:36) are today's semantics. Modular calls (D4) and k-induction (D5) change verdicts, so a diff could not tell a native bug from a semantics change. Swap the backend first; change semantics later, each with its own ADR.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aN"
    },
    {
      "id": "s_note_lock",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1002,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 384,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1865686222,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 493542218,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790760489337,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "sketchpactId": "s_note_lock",
        "owner": "simplicity"
      },
      "text": "LOCKED now: D3 one-shot .smt2\n(no runtime change;\nverifier.vow:283 already uses\nprocess_run). D4 inline. D5 BMC\nonly, --max-k-step. D6 Vec = SMT\narray + len, no capacity caps;\nString = len only, content ops\nSkipped. D10 fail-closed gate,\nopt-in --backend native. Assumes\nD1(b): checker in compiler/\nonly, no Rust twin. DEFERRED:\nstdin pipe (G3), Rust shim,\nmodular calls, k-induction,\nexact strings, recursion,\nhash-consing (G4).",
      "originalText": "LOCKED now: D3 one-shot .smt2 (no runtime change; verifier.vow:283 already uses process_run). D4 inline. D5 BMC only, --max-k-step. D6 Vec = SMT array + len, no capacity caps; String = len only, content ops Skipped. D10 fail-closed gate, opt-in --backend native. Assumes D1(b): checker in compiler/ only, no Rust twin. DEFERRED: stdin pipe (G3), Rust shim, modular calls, k-induction, exact strings, recursion, hash-consing (G4).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aO"
    },
